  "answer": "The May 2020 RFP lists these **core functions** for the pension fund consultant:\n\n- Help develop and maintain the investment policy statement.\n- Plan asset allocation annually and monitor it regularly.\n- Recommend changes when markets shift significantly, and alert the Board to concerns.\n- Research and recommend investments in each asset class.\n- Monitor recommended investments closely; meet with the Pension Board quarterly in person and monthly or as needed by phone.\n- Provide monthly portfolio-performance reports and statements.\n- Guide City staff on sourcing funds, opening accounts, and tracking liquidity for pension payments.\n- Coordinate with investment managers, funds, and custodians to ensure timely year-end financial reporting and quarterly updates.\n\nSource: *City of Creve Coeur Employee Pension Plan, Pension Fund Consulting Services RFP*, pp. 1–2.",
